aring or understanding what someone says  "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I didn't catch that. What did he say?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn2le08ob10aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to write down "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to write something on a piece of paper "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Let me write it down for you."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn2le08ob10aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to call back "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to return a phone call "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Sorry, I couldn't reach you. Please call me back."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn2le08ob10aud08"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn2le08ob10re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Present Simple Tense"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Use the Present Simple to talk about facts and usual actions."}, {"type": "text", "content": "To form the negative, use do / does not  before the verb. </br>Do not add s to the verb when used with he, she, it.</br> Pay attention to the short form. It's used in talking.</br></br>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "To form a yes/no question, use do/does and change the word order like this:         \tDo / Does + subject + verb </br>Do not add s to the verb with he, she, it."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I didn't catch the number."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Do you have a voicemail?"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Find a partner. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Pretend you have a voicemail you do not understand. Ask your partner questions about missing information from the voicemail, like the date and the place."}, {"type": 